===Pronunciation===
* {{a|British}} {{IPA|/ˈpɒtə/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-potter.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɒtə(r)|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|pottere}}, from late {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|pottere||potter}}, equivalent to {{suffix|pot|er|lang=en}}, influenced by {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|potier||potter}}. More at [[pot]]. Displaced {{etyl|ang|-}} {{m|ang|crocwyrhta||crock-wright}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# One who makes [[pot]]s and other [[ceramic]] [[ware]]s.
#* '''1961''', J. A. Philip, "Mimesis in the ''Sophistês'' of Plato," ''Transactions and Proceedings of the American Philological Association'', vol. 92, p. 453,
#*: shoemakers, weavers, '''potters''', bronzeworkers who produced and purveyed the articles necessary for daily life.
# {{context|idiomatic|biblical|lang=en}} [[God]], the [[creator]].
#* '''1611.''' ''Old Testament'', King James Version, Isaiah 64:8,
#*: But now, O Lord, thou art our Father; we are the clay, and thou art our '''potter'''; and we are the work of thy hand.
#* '''2011.''' ''Old Testament'', New International Version, Isaiah 64:8,
#*: Yet you, {{smallcaps|Lord}}, are our Father. We are the clay, you are the '''potter'''; we are all the work of your hand.
# One who places flowers or other plants inside their pots.
# One who [[pot]]s [[meat]]s or other [[eatable]]s.
# One who [[hawk]]s [[crockery]] or [[earthenware]].
#: {{rfquotek|De Quincey}}
# The {{vern|red-bellied terrapin}}, {{taxlink|Pseudemys rubriventris|species|noshow=1}}.
# {{taxlink|Deirochelys serrata|species|noshow=1}}.

